#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.dcf.short"
msgstr "Discounted cash flow valuation: the present value of future cash flows"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.dcf.ask"
msgstr "Explain DCF (discounted cash flow valuation) in one paragraph for a finance beginner. Cover the core idea, the 3 key inputs, and its biggest limitation."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.wacc.short"
msgstr "Weighted Average Cost of Capital — the discount rate used in a DCF"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.wacc.ask"
msgstr "What is WACC (Weighted Average Cost of Capital)? How is it calculated, and why is it the most sensitive input in a DCF model? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.pe.short"
msgstr "P/E ratio = price / earnings per share — how many years to earn back the price"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.pe.ask"
msgstr "How do you use the P/E ratio? Does a high P/E always mean expensive? Explain the correct usage in one paragraph."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ebitda.short"
msgstr "Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation & Amortization — operating profit stripped of financing and accounting effects"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ebitda.ask"
msgstr "What is EBITDA? Why do valuations often use EV/EBITDA instead of P/E? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.fcf.short"
msgstr "Free Cash Flow = operating cash flow − capital expenditure — the cash actually available to shareholders"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.fcf.ask"
msgstr "How does Free Cash Flow (FCF) differ from net income? Why do valuations favor FCF? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ev.short"
msgstr "Enterprise Value = market cap + net debt — the total cost to acquire the company"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ev.ask"
msgstr "What is Enterprise Value (EV)? Why not just use market cap? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.irr.short"
msgstr "Internal Rate of Return — the discount rate that makes NPV = 0, commonly used in LBOs"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.irr.ask"
msgstr "What does IRR (Internal Rate of Return) mean? In an LBO, is an 18% IRR high or low? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.lbo.short"
msgstr "Leveraged Buyout — buy a company with heavy debt, pay it down, then sell at a profit"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.lbo.ask"
msgstr "What does an LBO (Leveraged Buyout) model do? How does it differ from a DCF? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ddm.short"
msgstr "Dividend Discount Model — discounts future dividends into equity value"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ddm.ask"
msgstr "What kind of companies suit the DDM (Dividend Discount Model)? Why is it rarely used for tech stocks? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.beta.short"
msgstr "A stock's volatility relative to the market; beta = 1 moves in line with the market"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.beta.ask"
msgstr "What role does Beta play in CAPM? What does a beta of 0.8 vs 1.5 mean? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.roe.short"
msgstr "Return on Equity = net income / shareholders' equity — how efficiently shareholder capital earns returns"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.roe.ask"
msgstr "What ROE (Return on Equity) counts as excellent? How does it differ from ROA and ROIC? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.terminalValue.short"
msgstr "Terminal Value — the present value of all cash flows beyond the forecast period, typically 60–80% of total DCF value"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.terminalValue.ask"
msgstr "How is Terminal Value calculated in a DCF? Why does it have such a large impact on the result? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.pvOfFcf.short"
msgstr "The sum of the present values of free cash flows over the forecast period (discounted to today)"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.pvOfFcf.ask"
msgstr "What is PV of FCF (present value of free cash flow)? Why does a DCF discount future money back to today? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.enterpriseValue.short"
msgstr "Enterprise Value = equity + net debt — the cost to buy the entire company"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.enterpriseValue.ask"
msgstr "How does Enterprise Value differ from market cap? Why do valuations often use EV instead of market cap? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.equityValue.short"
msgstr "Equity Value = Enterprise Value − net debt — the portion belonging to shareholders"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.equityValue.ask"
msgstr "How do you convert between Equity Value and Enterprise Value? Which is more useful for an individual investor? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.evEbitda.short"
msgstr "Enterprise Value / operating profit — how many years of operating profit to earn back the value"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.evEbitda.ask"
msgstr "How do you use the EV/EBITDA multiple? What counts as cheap? How does it differ from P/E? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.beat.short"
msgstr "Beat — actual EPS above the analyst consensus estimate"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.beat.ask"
msgstr "Does an earnings beat always mean the stock will rise? Which details should you look at? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.miss.short"
msgstr "Miss — actual EPS below the analyst consensus estimate"

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.miss.ask"
msgstr "After an earnings miss, should you sell into the drop or buy the dip? Which details should you look at? Explain in one paragraph for a finance beginner."

#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "term.ariaLabel"
msgstr "Term: {term}"

